  "case": "cn-c-io-default-sets",
  "clause": "DESIGN R3.3 §7.1 Completion C (Sets); §16 item 8",
  "author": "spec-seal",
  "operation": "complete",
  "profile": "cn-c",
  "derivation": "The ID-less ioSpecification declares two inputs and one output and no sets. C creates one default InputSet and OutputSet whose ownerId is the explicitly evaluated Process id (never the ID-less parent): stable-id(Process_IO, input-set, default) and stable-id(Process_IO, output-set, default); membership is every declared IO id in UTF-16 order (DI_a before DI_b although declared second). The flowless Task_IO receives empty incoming/outgoing arrays (H F1). The assignRef of a created set is a write on a created element: source none/generated, result at <set>/dataInputRefs (H B9). Report header (H B4): sourceIdentity and targetIdentity are the envelope identity, inputRevision is baseRevision, outputRevision is revision.",
